WEBVTT

00:00:00.596 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.784 --> 00:00:04.990
In this lesson, we do a hybrid set, step by step:

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:08.589
mixing classic singles and volume fans on the same eye.

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:11.470
Throughout the set, remember three things:

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:17.163
the client's eyes stay closed, each single or fan goes on exactly one natural lash,

00:00:17.113 --> 00:00:19.230
and glue never touches the skin.

00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:20.594
Step one:

00:00:20.841 --> 00:00:22.834
consultation and choosing the look.

00:00:23.365 --> 00:00:27.074
Ask about allergies and about her eyes, as in the classic lesson.

00:00:27.504 --> 00:00:29.234
Then ask how she wants to look:

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.474
more natural, or a little fuller.

00:00:31.903 --> 00:00:34.514
Show her hybrid photos, and make it clear:

00:00:34.783 --> 00:00:38.754
this is a fluffy look, with defined lashes between soft fans.

00:00:38.932 --> 00:00:39.874
Agree right away:

00:00:40.048 --> 00:00:43.533
singles slightly longer than the fans, for a sharper look,

00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.434
or the same length or shorter, for a softer look.

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:47.794
Step two:

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:51.314
preparation, exactly as in the classic practice lesson:

00:00:51.661 --> 00:00:56.194
a comfortable position, cleansing, pads under the eyes, and brushing.

00:00:56.607 --> 00:00:59.394
If you have not seen it yet, watch that lesson first.

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:00.758
Step three:

00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:03.798
read the natural lashes, zone by zone.

00:01:04.302 --> 00:01:06.278
This is the deciding step of hybrid.

00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:10.758
Brush the lashes so they fluff up, then look closely at each zone:

00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:14.118
the inner corner, the middle, the outer corner.

00:01:14.623 --> 00:01:18.758
Lashes that are long, thick and strong are the places for fans.

00:01:19.184 --> 00:01:22.358
Lashes that are fine and short get a very light single.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.238
Baby lashes that are too weak stay bare.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.678
Watch for gaps too.

00:01:26.859 --> 00:01:30.358
Fans placed on the strong lashes around them will help cover the gaps.

00:01:30.603 --> 00:01:33.798
If you are not sure whether a lash is strong enough, go lighter.

00:01:34.213 --> 00:01:36.998
Too light, and you can add more at the next refill.

00:01:37.195 --> 00:01:40.038
Too heavy, and the natural lash pays the price.

00:01:40.716 --> 00:01:41.489
Step four:

00:01:41.738 --> 00:01:42.769
set up your station.

00:01:43.104 --> 00:01:45.489
For hybrid, you need both kinds of lashes:

00:01:45.754 --> 00:01:49.985
a tray of thicker classic lashes, and a tray of very fine volume lashes,

00:01:49.935 --> 00:01:51.089
arranged by length.

00:01:51.356 --> 00:01:53.729
A jade stone with a fresh drop of glue.

00:01:53.993 --> 00:01:54.849
And your tweezers:

00:01:55.038 --> 00:01:59.174
straight tweezers for isolating, curved tweezers for attaching singles,

00:01:59.124 --> 00:02:01.649
and angled volume tweezers for making fans.

00:02:01.918 --> 00:02:04.529
A lash wand and disposable cotton swabs.

00:02:04.835 --> 00:02:07.729
The glue bottle, capped straight after you take the glue.

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:09.264
Step five:

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.384
plan the lengths.

00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:14.384
Usually short at the inner corner, getting longer toward the outer corner.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.608
Drawing a style for each eye shape,

00:02:16.558 --> 00:02:19.264
we will learn in detail in the lash mapping lesson.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.584
With hybrid, also remember:

00:02:21.775 --> 00:02:25.644
choose the lengths for the singles and for the fans in each zone in advance,

00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:27.904
to match the look you agreed with the client.

00:02:28.227 --> 00:02:29.344
Keep the difference small.

00:02:30.022 --> 00:02:30.954
Step six:

00:02:31.096 --> 00:02:33.114
attach singles to the weaker lashes.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.634
With the straight tweezers in your non dominant hand, isolate a single natural lash.

00:02:39.064 --> 00:02:43.194
Choose a fine, short classic lash that this natural lash can carry.

00:02:43.704 --> 00:02:46.956
Touch the base of the extension to the edge of the glue drop,

00:02:46.906 --> 00:02:48.794
then lay it along the natural lash,

00:02:48.903 --> 00:02:51.914
about 0.5 to 1 mm from the eyelid skin.

00:02:52.258 --> 00:02:55.994
Hold still for a moment so the glue grabs, then release the tweezers.

00:02:56.588 --> 00:02:57.446
Step seven:

00:02:57.799 --> 00:03:00.086
attach fans to the strong lashes.

00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:03.046
Make the fans as in the volume practice lesson:

00:03:03.152 --> 00:03:06.806
a small, neat base, with the lashes spread evenly.

00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:10.806
In hybrid, you usually need only light fans with few lashes.

00:03:11.307 --> 00:03:13.446
Touch only the base of the fan to the glue.

00:03:13.795 --> 00:03:17.674
Then place the base so it wraps around the isolated natural lash,

00:03:17.624 --> 00:03:19.206
in the direction it grows,

00:03:19.393 --> 00:03:20.646
never touching the skin.

00:03:21.057 --> 00:03:21.606
Remember:

00:03:21.755 --> 00:03:24.326
fans are only for lashes strong enough to carry them.

00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:27.447
A very common mistake when you are new to hybrid:

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.370
because you keep switching between tweezers and two lash trays,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.727
your hands start to rush.

00:03:33.031 --> 00:03:36.967
So you pick up a thick classic lash by mistake, for a baby lash.

00:03:37.305 --> 00:03:40.087
Or you take more glue, worried the fan will not hold.

00:03:40.515 --> 00:03:41.607
The fix is simple.

00:03:41.876 --> 00:03:44.967
Give each lash tray a fixed spot, and never move it.

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:48.407
When you finish with a pair of tweezers, put it back in its own place.

00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:52.218
And before each attachment, look at the natural lash again,

00:03:52.168 --> 00:03:53.927
then choose a single or a fan.

00:03:54.573 --> 00:03:55.370
Step eight:

00:03:55.625 --> 00:03:57.450
alternate, and keep it even.

00:03:57.859 --> 00:04:01.290
Never attach all the fans first and the singles afterwards.

00:04:01.486 --> 00:04:02.709
Work zone by zone,

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:07.210
mixing singles and fans according to the natural lashes in that zone.

00:04:07.639 --> 00:04:12.533
As in the earlier lessons, never attach lashes that sit right next to each other,

00:04:12.483 --> 00:04:13.610
one after another:

00:04:13.782 --> 00:04:18.173
attach at the outer corner, then in the middle, then at the inner corner,

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.730
then go back, so the glue has time to cure.

00:04:21.159 --> 00:04:23.770
After each zone, step back and look:

00:04:24.119 --> 00:04:27.210
are the fans spread evenly, or bunching in one spot?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:28.655
Step nine:

00:04:28.983 --> 00:04:30.575
check for stickies and gaps.

00:04:31.002 --> 00:04:34.895
Glide the straight tweezers lightly through the lashes, from base to tip.

00:04:35.221 --> 00:04:39.775
Each single, each fan, must stand alone on a single natural lash.

00:04:40.123 --> 00:04:42.495
If you see a sticky, separate it right away.

00:04:42.925 --> 00:04:47.215
In hybrid, stickies often hide where a fan sits right next to a single:

00:04:47.484 --> 00:04:50.415
the outermost lash of the fan very easily touches it.

00:04:50.684 --> 00:04:52.735
Look from above, and from the side.

00:04:52.977 --> 00:04:57.135
Wherever there is still a gap, with a natural lash strong enough, fill it in.

00:04:57.792 --> 00:04:58.652
Step ten:

00:04:58.909 --> 00:05:00.252
compare both eyes.

00:05:00.748 --> 00:05:04.012
Sit at the head of the bed, and look down at both eyes at once.

00:05:04.361 --> 00:05:05.969
Length, fullness, curl,

00:05:05.919 --> 00:05:10.172
and the density at the outer corners must match on both sides.

00:05:10.596 --> 00:05:13.719
The natural lashes on the two sides are rarely identical,

00:05:13.669 --> 00:05:16.092
so the mix on each side can differ slightly.

00:05:16.437 --> 00:05:19.372
What must match is the look when the client opens her eyes.

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:20.888
Step eleven:

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:21.688
finishing.

00:05:22.222 --> 00:05:23.646
Brush the lashes again,

00:05:23.596 --> 00:05:27.768
remove the pads very gently while the client's eyes are still closed,

00:05:28.118 --> 00:05:29.928
then let her open her eyes slowly.

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:32.955
Give aftercare advice as in the classic lesson,

00:05:32.905 --> 00:05:35.528
and book a refill for two to three weeks later.

00:05:36.007 --> 00:05:39.879
Once the client has gone, single use items go into a lidded bin,

00:05:39.829 --> 00:05:42.328
and tweezers are cleaned and disinfected.

00:05:42.885 --> 00:05:46.497
Your first hybrid set will make you stop and think at every lash.

00:05:46.747 --> 00:05:47.697
That is a good thing.

00:05:48.096 --> 00:05:52.257
After many sets, your eyes will read natural lashes very quickly.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:55.137
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
